 "id": "07-s07-brain",
 "text": "And here's where things get even more interesting. Your brain isn't a fixed machine. It can adapt through learning. In brain-imaging research, people trained in echolocation showed increased responses to echoes in regions normally associated with vision. And this wasn't limited to people who were blind. Sighted participants showed changes too. That doesn't mean hearing has turned into eyesight. It means your brain can learn new ways of extracting information from sound.",
